  "marketing": {
    "about_hero_button": "See How The Hockey App Works",
    "about_hero_heading_gradient": "my family needed it.",
    "about_hero_heading_prefix": "I built this app because",
    "about_hero_p1": "I'm Jon Morrison. I coach in the Abbotsford Hawks organization and in spring hockey, and I have three daughters who play. I kept running into the same problem every family faces: getting kids to train at home without it turning into a fight. So I built something to fix it.",
    "about_img_alt_founder": "Jon Morrison coaching youth hockey",
    "about_img_alt_garage": "Young female hockey player training in her garage",
    "about_img_alt_kid_driveway": "Young hockey player practicing shooting in the driveway",
    "about_section_cta_get_started": "Get Started For Free",
    "about_section_cta_heading_gradient": "train at home.",
    "about_section_cta_heading_prefix": "The best players",
    "about_section_cta_p1": "The rink is where you compete. The garage, the basement, the driveway — that's where you get better. The players who separate themselves are the ones who put in the quiet reps when nobody's watching.",
    "about_section_cta_p2": "The Hockey App makes that training easy, fun, and something kids actually want to do. No nagging. No pressure. Just a clear plan and the motivation to show up every day.",
    "about_story_h2_built": "Why I Built This",
    "about_story_h2_daughters": "Three Daughters in the Game",
    "about_story_h2_pattern": "The Pattern I Kept Seeing",
    "about_story_h2_philosophy": "The Philosophy",
    "about_story_h2_started": "Where It Started",
    "about_story_h2_work": "The Work Behind the App",
    "about_story_h2_what_it_does": "What It Does",
    "about_story_p_built1": "The Hockey App exists because I needed it. As a coach, I needed a way to give families clear weekly plans without creating more work for parents. As a dad, I needed a system my daughters could follow on their own so training happened without me standing over them.",
    "about_story_p_built2": "This isn't a tech company's idea of what hockey needs. It's a coach and father's answer to a problem I've lived with for over a decade.",
    "about_story_p_daughters1": "I'm also a hockey dad. I have three daughters who play. I've lived the exact tension I'm describing: trying to support without pushing, trying to encourage without nagging, trying to build discipline without creating resentment.",
    "about_story_p_daughters2": "That's the hardest part of being a hockey parent: you care deeply, but if you push too hard, your child pulls away.",
    "about_story_p_pattern1": "Today I coach in the Abbotsford Hawks organization and in spring hockey. Over the years, I've coached U7, U9, and U11, along with development groups across the Fraser Valley. Working with players and families across different ages keeps this app grounded in what teams actually need.",
    "about_story_p_pattern2": "And I kept seeing the same pattern:",
    "about_story_p_pattern3": "Coaches would assign off-ice training. Parents would try to make it happen. Kids would resist. And every night, the same argument would play out in kitchens across the country: \"Did you do your training?\"",
    "about_story_p_pattern4": "The problem was never the kid's commitment. It was the lack of structure. There was no system. No clear plan. No way for the child to own it themselves.",
    "about_story_p_philosophy1": "I believe development happens through daily habits, not occasional intensity. I believe kids are more capable than we think, if we give them the structure to succeed. And I believe parents deserve to step back from being the enforcer and just be the supporter.",
    "about_story_p_philosophy2": "The Hockey App is designed around these beliefs. It's calm. It's structured. And it works because it removes friction instead of adding it.",
    "about_story_p_started1": "I grew up in the rink. I played junior hockey in the BCHL, lived in billets, trained year-round, and learned what it meant to be accountable to a team before I was old enough to vote.",
    "about_story_p_started2": "Hockey taught me structure. It taught me that talent matters less than consistency. And it taught me that the players who develop the fastest are the ones who do the quiet work: the unglamorous reps at home, in the garage, in the basement, when nobody is watching.",
    "about_story_p_get_clear": "At Get Clear Consulting, I help organizations find where work gets stuck and turn the right problems into practical software their teams will actually use. I brought the same approach to The Hockey App: listen to coaches and families, simplify the workflow, and build only what helps players keep showing up.",
    "about_story_p_what1": "The Hockey App gives coaches a simple way to assign structured off-ice training. Kids open the app, see their tasks for the day, and check them off. Parents get visibility without having to manage anything. Everyone stays aligned.",
    "about_story_p_what2": "No rankings. No pressure. No public leaderboards. Just quiet consistency, the kind that builds real athletes.",
    "about_why_teams_h2": "Why we built it for teams",
    "about_why_teams_p1": "Youth hockey has never been more competitive, and not just on the ice. Families weigh which program will actually develop their player, and strong players gravitate to teams that can show a real plan. Most coaches want to offer that and have no tool to do it. Practice ends, players go home, and development becomes a guess. We built The Hockey App so any program, at any level, can give players a structured plan between practices and prove the work is happening. That's how a program earns a reputation for development, and how it attracts and keeps the players who take it seriously.",
    "about_edge_line": "Whether you're running a AAA program or a house team, the goal is the same: give your players a system they can own, and give your program an edge it can show.",
    "about_families_line": "And families training on their own are welcome here too, the same program works for a single player as it does for a full roster.",
